#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Applies the Telegrios overlay onto a Nagram (NekoX-style) clone.

v1.3 — Telegrios: rebrand, Telegram-style icon, iOS themes, diagnostics v3:
  * Full rebrand: app name "Telegrios", applicationId org.telegrios.messenger,
    mod package org.telegram.telegrios (settings entry "Telegrios Settings").
  * New launcher icon in the style of the original Telegram (blue gradient
    circle + white paper plane): generated for all densities, adaptive layers,
    round icons, BOTH naming schemes (@mipmap/ic_launcher* and Nagram's
    @mipmap/ic_launcher_nagram*), plus the in-app logo drawable.
  * Three complete themes, switchable in "Telegrios Settings → Стиль темы":
    - Telegrios Dark (AMOLED black + neon green) — default;
    - iOS Light  — authentic Telegram-for-iPhone day palette (#F2F2F7 grouped
      surfaces, #007AFF accent, #E1FEC6 outgoing bubbles);
    - iOS Dark   — Telegram-for-iPhone night palette (#1C1C1E cards, #0A84FF,
      blue outgoing bubbles). The three .attheme files are also shipped in
      res/raw for sharing.
  * Crash diagnostics v3 (reliable this time):
    - Nagram installs a MAIN-THREAD specific UncaughtExceptionHandler in
      ApplicationLoader.attachBaseContext that swallows main-thread crashes
      before any default handler runs — this is why v1.2 never showed a report.
      The hook is now installed in attachBaseContext and the per-thread handler
      is wrapped so every crash is recorded.
    - Boot milestones (breadcrumbs) are written at every startup stage and
      survive native crashes / process kills; the report shows how far the
      previous launch got.
    - On any crash: trace saved → app re-opens into TelegriosCrashActivity
      (self-contained, shows report, share, save to Downloads, restart).
      If the previous session died before the UI was ready, the next launch
      starts in safe mode and shows the report instead of crashing again.
  * minifyEnabled/shrinkResources disabled for release (reflection-based mod).
  * APP_ID/APP_HASH regex hardened (does not touch OFFICIAL_APP_ID/TGX_APP_ID).

Usage:
    python3 apply_overlay.py --repo /path/to/Nagram [--app-id 12834 --app-hash c84d9...]

Idempotent: safe to re-run. Optional failures print WARN and never abort.
"""
